## Consume (shell)

| Method | Path | Purpose |
|--------|------|---------|
| `GET` | `/api/v1/notifications/inbox` | List (`page_count`, `page_offset`, `project=posif`) |
| `GET` | `/api/v1/notifications/inbox/unread-count` | Bell badge |
| `POST` | `/api/v1/notifications/inbox/{id}/read` | Mark one read |
| `POST` | `/api/v1/notifications/inbox/read-all` | Mark all read |

Auth: `Authorization: Bearer <JWT>`, permission `read:public`. Base: **`https://api.vtc.com`**.

**Realtime:** chat.vtc.com Socket.IO event **`notification:new`** (after JWT connect; socket joins `user:{userId}`). **Not** `ws.vtc.com`.

**Deep link:** prefer `payload.deep_link`; shell fallbacks for `invite` / `app_transfer` → `/dashboard/apps`.

---

## Child apps — what to do

1. **Need the chrome bell** → add/extend a **ZAPI platform service** that calls `NotificationDispatchService.create_and_deliver` (or propose a deliberate public create API first — none exists).
2. **Need user contact only** → email/SMS endpoints (`nextjs-to-vite.mdc`).
3. **Need live updates inside your app** → `ws.vtc.com` rooms (`realtime.mdc`).
4. **Never** rely on parent `postMessage` for the shell inbox.

